{
 "result": "maze.py is a padded-border BFS. It reads sys.stdin.buffer, pads the grid with a wall border into one bytearray, pre-marks walls in a visited bytearray, and runs a level-by-level list BFS with early exit when E is reached. It prints the shortest 4-neighbour path length, or -1 when there is no path or S/E is missing, and prints 0 when S equals E. It matches all three public samples (2008, -1, 78). The assay registered a baseline median of 4.17 with 2.4% noise, up about 45% from the deque version. I am resting here because further gains would be small and the energy is better returned to the stem cell.",
